# MediTrust — FINAL frontend piece: First-Run System Setup screen (`/setup`)

Context: all 15 core screens are already built and wired. The backend is complete and FROZEN —
do not modify anything under /lib, /app/api, /prisma, or proxy.ts. The only missing UI is the
one-time first-run flow that creates the first hospital + first admin account on an empty system.
Build exactly one new screen: `/setup`.

## /setup update — pre-flight status check (backend now supports it)
- On mount: `GET /api/bootstrap/status` (public, no auth) → `{ needsSetup: boolean }`.
| `GET /api/bootstrap/status` | public | — | `200 { needsSetup: boolean }` | — |
- `needsSetup === false` → do NOT render the form: show "This system is already
  initialized." + "Go to login" → /login (auto-redirect after ~1.5s is fine).
- `needsSetup === true` → render the setup form exactly as previously specced.
- Add a `checking` state: brief neutral loader while the status resolves; never
  flash the form before the check completes.
- KEEP the 403-on-submit handling as a race guard (setup completed by someone
  else between page load and submit).

## Backend contract (already implemented)
`POST /api/bootstrap` — public, but ONE-TIME ONLY (permanently disables itself after success).
Body:
{
  "hospitalName": string (min 2),
  "hospitalCode": string (2–10 chars, e.g. "LUTH"),
  "adminName": string (min 2),
  "adminEmail": valid email,
  "adminPassword": string (strength rule below)
}
Success: `201 { message, healthId }` where healthId = "<HOSPITALCODE>-ADM-0001".
Errors:
- `403 { error: "bootstrap_already_completed" }` — an admin already exists; the endpoint is dead forever.
- `400 { error: "invalid_request", details }` — validation failed; `details` is a Zod flatten (use for field-level messages, especially password strength).
- `409 { error: "hospital_code_exists" | "email_exists" }`.
Behaviour notes:
- NO session is issued. The new admin then logs in through the normal two-step flow (password → OTP).
- The created admin has mustChangePassword = false (they chose their own strong password).
- Password strength rule (same as everywhere else): 10+ chars, upper, lower, number, symbol. Enforce client-side for instant feedback; server is the real gate.
- hospitalCode is uppercased server-side and prefixes all Health IDs / patient codes.
- Dev only: the login OTP is printed to the `pnpm dev` server console.

## Screen spec — `/setup` ("System Setup")
Who: unauthenticated, first run only. Standalone centered layout, same shell as Login —
no sidebar, no links to it from any authenticated screen (operational URL only).
Form (single column):
1. Hospital name
2. Hospital code (helper text: "Prefix for Health IDs and patient codes, e.g. LUTH")
3. Admin full name
4. Admin email
5. Admin password + confirm, with live strength checklist (10+ chars / upper / lower / number / symbol)
Submit: "Initialize system" (Deep Indigo #2B3A67).
States:
- default / submitting (button disabled + spinner)
- 400 → field-level errors from `details`; strength failures shown inline before/with submit
- 409 → banner "That hospital code or email is already in use."
- 403 → replace form with notice "This system is already initialized." + "Go to login" → /login
  (there is no status/probe endpoint by design; detecting via submit is the intended path)
- success → replace form with a success panel:
  - "System initialized."
  - The returned `healthId` in IBM Plex Mono, prominent, with copy button and one-time warning:
    "Save this Health ID now — it is shown only once."
  - Note: "Log in with this Health ID, your email, and the password you just set. A one-time
    code will be delivered (dev: printed to the server console)."
  - Primary CTA "Continue to login" → /login
Motion: only the success confirmation; nothing decorative. Type/colors: existing design system.

## Rules
- If an authenticated user visits /setup, redirect to their dashboard (same session check as Login).
- Never persist or echo the password beyond form state.
- No new dependencies.

## Verify
1. Empty DB (`pnpm prisma migrate reset`, skip seed): /setup → submit → success panel with Health ID → log in via /login with OTP from dev console.
2. Seeded DB (`pnpm db:seed`): any /setup submit → 403 notice → /login unchanged.
3. Weak password → inline strength errors; 409/400 paths render correctly.